{"stage": "review", "action": "scientific_findings", "result": {"verdict": "revise", "findings": ["The 'Total probability' metric is computed as traj[last] + (1 - traj[last]), which is identically 1 by construction and does not verify conservation of the actual two-component distribution; it is a tautology, not a meaningful numerical output. It should report the sum of the actual state distribution [p, 1-p] (still 1, but derived from the computed p) or better, verify that the row-stochastic matrix rows sum to 1 and that the update preserves normalization.", "The 'Non-convergent regime' message is only reached when factor === 1, but the code's else branch claims 'contraction factor ... equals 1' for any non-convergent case. Since factor = |1-a-b| and a,b in [0,1], factor can equal 1 only when a+b=0 or a+b=2, so the message is technically correct, but the branch ordering means a=b=0 and a=b=1 are handled first; the remaining factor===1 cases are a=0,b=0 (handled) and a=1,b=1 (handled), so the else branch is actually unreachable for valid inputs. This is dead code, not a correctness bug, but the message text is misleading if reached.", "The exploration 'Stable equilibrium' claims 'each deviation shrink by a factor of 10' with a=0.3, b=0.6, but the contraction factor is |1-0.3-0.6| = 0.1, so deviations shrink by a factor of 10 per step — this is correct. However, the 'observe' text says 'the contraction factor |1-0.3-0.6|=0.1 makes each deviation shrink by a factor of 10' which is accurate. No issue here."], "reference_tests": [{"name": "Stationary value for a=0.3, b=0.6", "state": {"p0": 0.9, "a": 0.3, "b": 0.6, "steps": 20}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.3.value", "value": 0.6666666666666666, "atol": 1e-09}]}, {"name": "Identity transition keeps p_0", "state": {"p0": 0.42, "a": 0, "b": 0, "steps": 20}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 0.42, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.2.value", "value": 1, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Deterministic flip alternates", "state": {"p0": 0.9, "a": 1, "b": 1, "steps": 1}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 0.1, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Symmetric chain halves the gap", "state": {"p0": 1, "a": 0.5, "b": 0.5, "steps": 1}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 0.5, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "value": 0.5, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Total probability conserved", "state": {"p0": 0.2, "a": 0.7, "b": 0.1, "steps": 20}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 1, "atol": 1e-12}]}], "invariants": [{"name": "Probability normalization", "expression": "Math.abs(o.metrics[0].value + (1 - o.metrics[0].value) - 1) < 1e-12"}, {"name": "Stationary point satisfies fixed-point equation", "expression": "!o.metrics[3] || Math.abs((1 - s.a) * o.metrics[3].value + s.b * (1 - o.metrics[3].value) - o.metrics[3].value) < 1e-12"}, {"name": "Contraction factor matches definition", "expression": "Math.abs(o.metrics[2].value - Math.abs(1 - s.a - s.b)) < 1e-12"}, {"name": "Trajectory stays in [0,1]", "expression": "o.panels[0].series[0].points.every(pt => pt[1] >= -1e-12 && pt[1] <= 1 + 1e-12)"}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 69.328}
